WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.170
<v Krista>In this video, we're talking about multiplication</v>

2
00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:03.530
of scientific notation.

3
00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:04.870
And in this particular example,

4
00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.030
we have four times 10 to the negative four

5
00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:09.250
times two times 10 to the 14.

6
00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:11.410
When you're multiply scientific notation like this,

7
00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.710
you always want to multiply the whole numbers together

8
00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:16.940
and then separately, multiply together these powers of 10.

9
00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:18.040
So in other words,

10
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.620
we're going to grab the four, this whole number,

11
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.550
and the two, the other whole number,

12
00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:24.020
and we're going to multiply those together

13
00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.940
so we're going to say four times two.

14
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.420
Then separately, we're going to grab the powers of 10,

15
00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:32.270
10 to the negative four and 10 to the 14,

16
00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:33.890
and we're going to multiply those together

17
00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:37.870
so 10 to the negative four times 10 to to the 14.

18
00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.380
So we just separate 'em like that.

19
00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.260
Now, you're going to get four times two,

20
00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:42.700
which is going to give you eight,

21
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:46.730
and then here, 10 to the negative four times 10 to the 14,

22
00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:49.090
well, we have like bases; the bases are 10,

23
00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:51.670
and when we have like bases that we're multiplying together,

24
00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:53.120
we just add the exponents.

25
00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:57.180
So negative four plus a 14 is going to be a positive 10

26
00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:02.180
so what we end up with is eight times 10 to the positive 10

27
00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.850
and that's our final answer in scientific notation.

28
00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.520
Let's do another example here.

29
00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.810
We've got a whole number of four

30
00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:10.980
and a whole number of three,

31
00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:14.310
and then we have powers of 10; 10 to the negative five

32
00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:17.120
and 10 to the negative eight, like this,

33
00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.363
so we're going to take four times three,

34
00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:22.240
and then separately, we're going to take the powers of 10;

35
00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:27.140
10 to the negative five times 10 to the negative eight.

36
00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:28.490
Now we're going to do four times three,

37
00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:30.180
which is going to give us 12,

38
00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:31.740
and then we're going to multiply that

39
00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.950
by 10 to the negative times 10 to the negative eight.

40
00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:36.430
We can add the exponents.

41
00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:38.870
Negative five plus a negative eight is the same as

42
00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:42.340
negative five minus eight, which will be negative 13,

43
00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:45.180
so we'll get 10 to the negative 13.

44
00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.340
But even though we've multiplied our whole numbers together

45
00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.940
and our powers of 10 together, we still need to realize

46
00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:52.800
that our final answer is not yet in scientific notation.

47
00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.710
Remember that in scientific notation,

48
00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.870
we can't have this two-digit whole number here.

49
00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:59.450
We have to have a one-digit whole number plus a decimal.

50
00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:01.690
This is essentially 12.0.

51
00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:04.110
We need to move this decimal one unit to the left

52
00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:05.920
so that we get 1.2.

53
00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.270
When we do that, we'll end up with

54
00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:11.090
1.2 times 10 to the positive one

55
00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:13.690
because we moved the decimal one spot to the left.

56
00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:17.400
So one spot means 10 to the first, and it's positive one

57
00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.900
because we moved the decimal to the left.

58
00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:21.680
Then we have times 10 to the negative 13,

59
00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.950
and now we just need to combine our powers of 10.

60
00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:28.250
So we end up with 1.2 times, adding the exponents together,

61
00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:31.090
positive one and negative 13 gives us a negative 12

62
00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:34.243
so we get times 10 to the negative 12.

